From ba5bdf9b9f384509a1c75118e2744170b6dcbfea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:35:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/53] B70-V2-MOE: EP sentinel + rows_per_expert zero in one
 Triton kernel, dead padding mask dropped (B70_MOE_KCUT=1)

After the EP sentinel rewrite every topk id is >= 0, so the (ids<0).all(1) + masked_fill in
XpuFusedMoe._apply_kernel and the W4A8 cutlass apply is the identity. One launch replaces
compare/fill/where + compare/reduce/D2D/masked_fill + zeros: 7 kernels per MoE layer, 336 per
c=1 step. Replicas of the wheel bodies arm only on a matching AST fingerprint (v6).
Default off; bitwise-identical (CPU tests, NaN padding rows included).
